/// Real outturn from the 31 OSCAR in-year releases as revision deltas: one row for each change a release makes to a line (organisation version, sub-segment, economic category, control budget detail, period), only non-zero deltas. The sum of the deltas up to a release equals what that release reports. GBP thousands, spending positive, income negative. Source view dw.v_model_fact_outturn.
table 'Fact Outturn'
	lineageTag: cb607bbf-daa1-5cc8-a027-41f68dfb1127

	/// Real outturn in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative: the sum of the revision deltas of every release in context. With no release selected it is the latest view of each financial year (what the newest release reports). It never filters releases itself, so a view as at a release is a selection on Release. Not on the plan basis: all control budgets and economic categories. Use Outturn (plan basis) to compare with a plan.
	measure Outturn = SUM ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Base
		lineageTag: a9b46f48-e2ea-5ade-a3d6-848f0441008f

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["AVOID_DUPLICATE_MEASURES"]}

	/// Outturn in GBP thousands on the basis of the plan rows in context, the figure that Plan is compared with. For each financial year and plan measure in context it takes the outturn of the control budget detail and economic budget the measure is made of (RDEL, RDEL_EX_DEPN, CDEL, RAME, CAME, ADMIN, ADMIN_EX_DEPN, and my own rules for NON_DEPT_AME, NON_BUDGET and UNCLASSIFIED) and adds them up. Resource DEL excluding depreciation leaves out only the economic group DEPRECIATION, because the in-year files have no ringfence column; other non-cash items stay in (about 5.5bn a year from 2024-25). BLANK when there is no plan row in context. Defined at every grain, including months, where Plan is BLANK.
	measure 'Outturn (plan basis)' =
			VAR MeasureChosen = ISFILTERED ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] )
			VAR PlanScope =
			    SUMMARIZE (
			        FILTER ( 'Fact Plan', MeasureChosen || NOT 'Fact Plan'[Is Part Of Other Measure] ),
			        'Fiscal Year'[Financial Year],
			        'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure]
			    )
			VAR AnyWithoutRule =
			    COUNTROWS ( FILTER ( PlanScope, NOT Basis.HasRule ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] ) ) ) > 0
			RETURN
			    IF (
			        AnyWithoutRule,
			        BLANK (),
			        SUMX ( PlanScope, Basis.OutturnFor ( 'Fiscal Year'[Financial Year], 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] ) )
			    )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: bd6cb56a-9d8e-5fe4-be25-5820174c8dce

	/// The measure to put in a visual together with the Scenario Comparison items. On its own it is Outturn (plan basis), the Actual of a comparison. The Scenario Comparison items act only on this measure and pass every other measure through unchanged.
	measure 'Comparison Amount' = [Outturn (plan basis)]
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: 58ace511-bcb8-56ae-a51f-1b03c1102e4d

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["MEASURES_SHOULD_NOT_BE_DIRECT_REFERENCES_OF_OTHER_MEASURES"]}

	/// The group income and expenditure statement: the outturn of the statement line in context, in GBP thousands, in the sign the line is presented in (income lines positive, the net and total lines as reported, spending positive). A detail line sums the accounts the authored rules give it; a subtotal or total sums the detail lines under the lines it lists; a spacer, and a context with more than one line, give BLANK. The total line equals Outturn. Put Statement Line[Line] on rows; Control Budget on columns splits it into DEL, AME and non-budget.
	measure 'Statement Amount' = Pnl.LineAmount ( [Outturn] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement
		lineageTag: 70206046-b61e-459a-90f0-c608a41263df

	/// The statement amount on the plan's basis, only where the line has a plan (the net resource line, the net capital line and the total line, in a year the source gives a plan at that level): for each voted budget the year has, the outturn of the control budget detail and economic budget it is made of, within the line's economic budget. This is the Actual that Variance is taken against; BLANK where Statement Plan is BLANK.
	measure 'Statement Amount (plan basis)' = IF ( ISBLANK ( [Statement Plan] ), BLANK (), Pnl.AtPlanScope ( [Comparison Amount] ) )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement
		lineageTag: 8e1ac7fe-1ca9-478b-ac5b-f5c5385d3da3

	/// Statement amount on the plan's basis less the plan, GBP thousands, in the sign the line is presented in. With spending positive, below zero is favourable. BLANK where either side is BLANK.
	measure 'Statement Variance' =
			VAR Actual = [Statement Amount (plan basis)]
			VAR PlanAmount = [Statement Plan]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( Actual ) || ISBLANK ( PlanAmount ), BLANK (), Actual - PlanAmount )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement
		lineageTag: 7160b5a6-803a-4674-bec3-ab61caf0c00a

	/// Statement variance divided by the absolute statement plan. BLANK where the plan is zero or either side is BLANK.
	measure 'Statement Variance %' =
			VAR Actual = [Statement Amount (plan basis)]
			VAR PlanAmount = [Statement Plan]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( Actual ) || ISBLANK ( PlanAmount ), BLANK (), DIVIDE ( Actual - PlanAmount, ABS ( PlanAmount ) ) )
		formatString: 0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%
		displayFolder: Statement
		lineageTag: a62e1436-3f3c-4715-bb02-34569ff3eff9

	/// The statement amount of the previous financial year, by OFFSET over the Fiscal Year table in order of year start (the year before in the table, whatever a slicer selects). Use it at year grain; BLANK for the first year and for a year the previous year of which has no outturn.
	measure 'Statement Amount PY (OFFSET)' =
			CALCULATE (
			    [Statement Amount],
			    OFFSET ( -1, ALL ( 'Fiscal Year'[Financial Year], 'Fiscal Year'[Year Start] ), ORDERBY ( 'Fiscal Year'[Year Start], ASC ) )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement\Windows
		lineageTag: 76a329b5-881e-44ba-81a2-b55c2e4d0298

	/// The statement amount added up from period 0 to the period in context within each financial year, by WINDOW over Fiscal Period (a running total that restarts every year). Use it with Fiscal Period[Financial Year] and Fiscal Period[Period Number] on the visual.
	measure 'Statement Amount Running (WINDOW)' =
			CALCULATE (
			    [Statement Amount],
			    WINDOW (
			        1, ABS, 0, REL,
			        ALLSELECTED ( 'Fiscal Period'[Financial Year], 'Fiscal Period'[Period Number] ),
			        ORDERBY ( 'Fiscal Period'[Period Number], ASC ),
			        PARTITIONBY ( 'Fiscal Period'[Financial Year] )
			    )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement\Windows
		lineageTag: 99df98a7-f0a8-4169-8f3d-bea3dcafddda

	/// The statement amount of the period in context and the two before it, by WINDOW over the allocated months (period 1 to 12) of every year in order, so the window crosses the year end. Period 0 is not a month: it gets BLANK and is not in anyone's window. Use it with Fiscal Period[Financial Year] and Fiscal Period[Period Number] on the visual.
	measure 'Statement Amount Moving 3 Months (WINDOW)' =
			CALCULATE (
			    [Statement Amount],
			    WINDOW (
			        -2, REL, 0, REL,
			        FILTER ( ALLSELECTED ( 'Fiscal Period'[Period Key], 'Fiscal Period'[Period Number] ), 'Fiscal Period'[Period Number] >= 1 ),
			        ORDERBY ( 'Fiscal Period'[Period Key], ASC )
			    ),
			    REMOVEFILTERS ( 'Fiscal Year' ),
			    REMOVEFILTERS ( 'Fiscal Period'[Financial Year], 'Fiscal Period'[Period Number] )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement\Windows
		lineageTag: 2cf94197-3e63-4495-849a-04ad3ba85a59

	/// Rank of the department in context among the departments that have a statement amount in the context (1 is the largest amount; equal amounts share a rank and the next rank is skipped), by RANK over the departments of the current structure. Put Department (current structure)[Department] on rows and one statement line and year in the filter context.
	measure 'Department Rank (Statement Amount)' =
			IF (
			    ISBLANK ( [Statement Amount] ),
			    BLANK (),
			    RANK (
			        SKIP,
			        FILTER ( ALLSELECTED ( 'Department (current structure)' ), NOT ISBLANK ( [Statement Amount] ) ),
			        ORDERBY ( [Statement Amount], DESC )
			    )
			)
		formatString: 0
		displayFolder: Statement\Windows
		lineageTag: c346715c-2368-4376-bdd6-db48539f9174

	/// The outturn as the selected release stated it, in GBP thousands (spending positive, income negative): the sum of the revision deltas of every release up to and including the highest release in context, or up to the latest release when none is selected. For a year the release has not reached yet it is BLANK, and for a closed year it is the final figure known at that release. At a release's own financial year it equals what that release's file reports (tested against the control totals of the files). Written in the plain form, a CALCULATE over a FILTER of all releases; a later rewrite is compared with it.
	measure 'Outturn as at Release' =
			VAR AsAt = MAX ( 'Release'[Release Sequence] )
			RETURN
			    CALCULATE ( [Outturn], FILTER ( ALL ( 'Release' ), 'Release'[Release Sequence] <= AsAt ) )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: 10385ac7-fa5d-59c8-962f-c33bd7b749c8

	/// The outturn as first reported, in GBP thousands: the sum of the deltas with Revision Number 0, that is the amount each line and month had in the release that first reported it, over the releases up to the as-at release (the highest release in context, or the latest). A line first reported later is counted at its first amount, so this is not the total of the first release of the year.
	measure 'Outturn as First Reported' =
			VAR AsAt = MAX ( 'Release'[Release Sequence] )
			RETURN
			    CALCULATE ( [Outturn], 'Fact Outturn'[Revision Number] = 0, FILTER ( ALL ( 'Release' ), 'Release'[Release Sequence] <= AsAt ) )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: ab7d34bc-7082-5cc1-bcef-29cbcc3f45f1

	/// How much the outturn has moved since each line and month was first reported, in GBP thousands: Outturn as at Release less Outturn as First Reported, which is the sum of the deltas with a Revision Number above 0 up to the as-at release. Positive means spending grew or income fell since first reported. BLANK where neither side has a value, 0 where nothing was restated.
	measure 'Revision since First Reported' =
			VAR AtRelease = [Outturn as at Release]
			VAR FirstReported = [Outturn as First Reported]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( AtRelease ) && ISBLANK ( FirstReported ), BLANK (), AtRelease - FirstReported )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: 42a137d3-3796-5e56-b699-b0dae6611106

	/// Revision since First Reported as a share of the absolute outturn as first reported. BLANK where nothing was first reported or the first-reported amount is zero. Not an additive measure: a total is the ratio of the totals. Needs no data-quality exclusion: the NHS Pension Scheme unit error and its offsetting line net to a small amount, and both are flagged, so a view that left out only one of them would make the ratio worse, not better.
	measure 'Revision %' =
			VAR FirstReported = [Outturn as First Reported]
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE ( [Revision since First Reported], ABS ( FirstReported ) )
		formatString: 0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: fdb9d6dd-5028-5608-8f8c-37b34f271531

	/// The change the release or releases in context made to the year-to-date outturn, in GBP thousands: the sum of their deltas, which is what Outturn shows when Release is on rows. It is a movement, not a total, and it mixes months reported for the first time with restatements of months already reported (Restatement in Release is the second part alone). With no release selected it is the sum over all releases, which equals Outturn.
	measure 'Revision in Release' = SUM ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: f68ff81a-d6ce-5c8e-9b49-04d73b05d34e

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["AVOID_DUPLICATE_MEASURES"]}

	/// The part of Revision in Release that changes a figure an earlier release had already reported, in GBP thousands: the deltas with a Revision Number above 0. It is the restatement proper; a delta with Revision Number 0 is a month or line reported for the first time.
	measure 'Restatement in Release' = CALCULATE ( SUM ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] ), 'Fact Outturn'[Revision Number] > 0 )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: f45f68a7-eab3-5a5e-8fa0-1b3b1482a4c9

	/// The size of everything the release or releases in context changed, in GBP thousands: the sum of the absolute deltas, so increases and decreases do not net off. It includes lines reported for the first time, so in the first release of a year it is the size of the whole year to date. It counts the rows flagged in Data Quality Issue (the NHS Pension Scheme unit error and its offsetting line), which run to trillions in two releases: the excluding-flagged-rows variant leaves them out.
	measure 'Gross Revision in Release' = SUMX ( 'Fact Outturn', ABS ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] ) )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: 6492b5a0-42f2-5079-92e2-f9c4425f0d71

	/// The size of what the release or releases in context restated, in GBP thousands: the sum of the absolute deltas with a Revision Number above 0, so a restatement upward on one line and downward on another do not net off. The measure for how much was restated, as against how much moved. The rows flagged in Data Quality Issue (the NHS Pension Scheme unit error and its offsetting line) are counted here, trillions in two releases: see the excluding-flagged-rows variant.
	measure 'Gross Restatement in Release' = CALCULATE ( SUMX ( 'Fact Outturn', ABS ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] ) ), 'Fact Outturn'[Revision Number] > 0 )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement
		lineageTag: 018b364b-f4e1-58f4-b9a5-44074a55147a

	/// Gross Revision in Release with the rows flagged in Data Quality Issue left out (the thirteen delta rows of the two NHS Pension Scheme lines that carry a unit error, X903A002 and its offsetting line X903A003). What is left out is each flagged line-month as a whole, from the release that set the wrong amount to the release that corrected it, so the genuine amounts netted into the offsetting line in those months go too. Use it for the gross restatement page; the net measures need no exclusion.
	measure 'Gross Revision in Release (excl. flagged)' = Restate.Unflagged ( [Gross Revision in Release] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement\Excluding flagged rows
		lineageTag: f2de9b52-8606-5460-b63f-04fe82b33f1a

	/// Gross Restatement in Release with the rows flagged in Data Quality Issue left out (the thirteen delta rows of the two NHS Pension Scheme lines that carry a unit error, X903A002 and its offsetting line X903A003). What is left out is each flagged line-month as a whole, from the release that set the wrong amount to the release that corrected it, so the genuine amounts netted into the offsetting line in those months go too. Use it for the gross restatement page; the net measures need no exclusion.
	measure 'Gross Restatement in Release (excl. flagged)' = Restate.Unflagged ( [Gross Restatement in Release] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Restatement\Excluding flagged rows
		lineageTag: add26219-f7fa-53b1-aac5-819c818e0b3f

	/// Outturn in GBP thousands by the department of today's structure: the sum of the deltas of the lines that belong to the department in context (Fact Outturn is related to Department (current structure) on the department key written in the warehouse, and each department has one number). With Department (current structure) on rows. Equal to Outturn there; it is named so that a matrix holding both structures says which figure is which.
	measure 'Outturn (current structure)' = SUM ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Current Structure
		lineageTag: f03cb177-edf7-5935-bf2d-b27c410fa2a7

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["AVOID_DUPLICATE_MEASURES"]}

	/// Outturn in GBP thousands of the lines that the releases in context reported under the department number of the row, whatever department those lines belong to today. The counterpart of a row of Department (current structure) is found by number, never by name: the numbers that a department answers for are in its hidden column Reported Department Numbers (its own number; for Unallocated U011, U035 and U077 the number after the U; and for the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office also 027, the Foreign and Commonwealth Office). A selection on the as-reported department is kept, so it can only narrow. With Department (current structure) on rows. Added over all departments it equals Outturn.
	measure 'Outturn (as reported structure)' =
			VAR NumberLists = VALUES ( 'Department (current structure)'[Reported Department Numbers] )
			VAR Numbers =
			    FILTER (
			        ALL ( 'Organisation (as reported)'[Department Number (as reported)] ),
			        COUNTROWS (
			            FILTER (
			                NumberLists,
			                CONTAINSSTRING (
			                    'Department (current structure)'[Reported Department Numbers],
			                    "|" & 'Organisation (as reported)'[Department Number (as reported)] & "|"
			                )
			            )
			        ) > 0
			    )
			RETURN
			    CALCULATE (
			        [Outturn],
			        REMOVEFILTERS ( 'Department (current structure)' ),
			        KEEPFILTERS ( TREATAS ( Numbers, 'Organisation (as reported)'[Department Number (as reported)] ) )
			    )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Current Structure
		lineageTag: 256ac1e5-de9a-5a57-b366-c67e1f933b72

	/// What the change of structure moved into the department, in GBP thousands: Outturn (current structure) less Outturn (as reported structure). Positive means the department holds more today than it was reported with; negative means lines it was reported with now sit in another department. Added over all departments of the current structure it is zero (tested for every year and release). BLANK where both are BLANK.
	measure 'Machinery of Government Transfer' =
			VAR CurrentStructure = [Outturn (current structure)]
			VAR AsReported = [Outturn (as reported structure)]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( CurrentStructure ) && ISBLANK ( AsReported ), BLANK (), CurrentStructure - AsReported )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Current Structure
		lineageTag: e0fe938e-59d5-5e79-9252-34a1e3bdb78a

	/// The part of the outturn, in GBP thousands, that sits in its current department because of an estimated mapping: the lines marked is_estimated in the current-structure map (three BEIS lines placed by judgement and not by a published source). BLANK where the department has none.
	measure 'Outturn (estimated mapping)' = CALCULATE ( SUM ( 'Fact Outturn'[Amount Delta] ), 'Fact Outturn'[Mapping Is Estimated] = TRUE () )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Current Structure
		lineageTag: b646649a-ffac-50bc-9420-6cc13da61415

	/// The share of the outturn in context that comes from lines mapped to the current department by an estimated driver: Outturn (estimated mapping) over Outturn (current structure), on net amounts. 0 where the department has outturn and no estimated line; BLANK where it has no outturn or the net outturn is zero. On net amounts it can exceed 100% or be negative where the department's net outturn is small; read it with the amount.
	measure 'Estimated Mapping Share' =
			VAR Total = [Outturn (current structure)]
			RETURN
			    IF ( ISBLANK ( Total ), BLANK (), DIVIDE ( COALESCE ( [Outturn (estimated mapping)], 0 ), Total ) )
		formatString: 0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%
		displayFolder: Current Structure
		lineageTag: aa1c87b0-44b4-51fe-a94b-ea05ff838103

	/// Rank of the Spending Review group in context among the groups that have a value, by the year-to-date variance % (the Variance % item of Scenario Comparison under the YTD item of Time Intelligence, taken on Comparison Amount), the largest first (1 is the biggest overspend against plan); equal values share a rank and the next rank is skipped. BLANK where the group has no plan or no outturn on the plan's basis. The plan is published by group, not by current department, so the rank is over Spending Review groups. A year-to-date plan exists only at period 12 or for a whole year, so a month before the year end gives BLANK. Written in the plain form: the full CALCULATE with both items inside RANKX. Use it with no Time Intelligence or Scenario Comparison item selected.
	measure 'Department Group Rank (YTD Variance %)' =
			VAR YtdVariancePercent =
			    CALCULATE ( [Comparison Amount], 'Time Intelligence'[Time Calculation] = "YTD", 'Scenario Comparison'[Comparison] = "Variance %" )
			RETURN
			    IF (
			        ISBLANK ( YtdVariancePercent ),
			        BLANK (),
			        RANKX (
			            FILTER (
			                ALLSELECTED ( 'Spending Review Group' ),
			                NOT ISBLANK (
			                    CALCULATE ( [Comparison Amount], 'Time Intelligence'[Time Calculation] = "YTD", 'Scenario Comparison'[Comparison] = "Variance %" )
			                )
			            ),
			            CALCULATE ( [Comparison Amount], 'Time Intelligence'[Time Calculation] = "YTD", 'Scenario Comparison'[Comparison] = "Variance %" ),
			            ,
			            DESC,
			            SKIP
			        )
			    )
		formatString: 0
		displayFolder: Plan\Ranking
		lineageTag: 88d10e9b-1bad-57dc-8f49-98c96fd6f2cc

	/// [Outturn] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Outturn (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Outturn] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: bd4c09eb-0549-436a-b04f-60ff629a62ad

	/// [Outturn (plan basis)] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Outturn (plan basis) (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Outturn (plan basis)] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: 74787b84-b629-41f9-b930-8bc70db512f3

	/// [Outturn (current structure)] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Outturn (current structure) (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Outturn (current structure)] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: e79add6e-f965-4821-b7f0-62280a2284ee

	/// The month of the latest OSCAR in-year release in the model, for example Sep 2026, whatever is selected. A label for page headers; it holds no amount.
	measure 'Latest Release in View' = MAXX ( FILTER ( ALL ( Release ), Release[Is Latest Release] = TRUE () ), Release[Release] )
		displayFolder: Report Labels
		lineageTag: 1a0b1fea-7a20-5958-a81f-577d0c3611f4

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["UKFR_MEASURE_FOLDER_AND_FORMAT","UKFR_MEASURE_FORMAT_IN_SET"]}

	/// [Statement Amount] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Statement Amount (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Statement Amount] )
